WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.320
The first film ended with many small cells sharing the job list.

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.080
So who gets oxygen to the cells in your toes, far from your lungs?

3
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.120
Those toe cells need it right now.

4
00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.513
Follow that one job.

5
00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:20.373
It starts with one kind of cell.

6
00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:25.893
A red blood cell is a small, flexible disc, dented on both sides.

7
00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.213
It carries oxygen.

8
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:34.097
A cell whose shape and parts suit it to one kind of job is called a specialized

9
00:00:34.097 --> 00:00:40.257
cell. In mammals, including humans, a mature red blood cell has no nucleus.

10
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.810
Here is a blood vessel narrower than the red blood cell.

11
00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.390
What would let the cell get through?

12
00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.710
Pause and decide.

13
00:00:56.267 --> 00:01:02.787
Its shape. The flexible disc bends and folds, squeezes through the very narrow

14
00:01:02.787 --> 00:01:05.187
vessel, and springs back on the other side.

15
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.910
But blood has to be pushed.

16
00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.350
That job belongs to heart muscle cells.

17
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.750
Each one is striped, and it shortens to squeeze.

18
00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:19.113
Many heart muscle cells link up into a network.

19
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:22.733
Similar cells doing one job form a tissue.

20
00:01:24.073 --> 00:01:27.333
This one is heart muscle tissue, and its cells shorten together.

21
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:31.997
Heart muscle tissue works together with other kinds of tissue.

22
00:01:33.277 --> 00:01:36.297
Different tissues working together form an organ, the heart.

23
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:41.810
The heart pushes blood, fresh from the lungs, through a branching set of blood

24
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:46.210
vessels. Organs working together form an organ system.

25
00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.370
The heart and blood vessels are one.

26
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:53.513
All the systems together make the organism, you.

27
00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:57.153
Now the oxygen reaches the cells in your toes.

28
00:01:58.473 --> 00:02:02.073
That one job took every level, from one cell to the whole body.

29
00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.793
Other cells have other shapes for other jobs.

30
00:02:07.073 --> 00:02:08.713
A nerve cell has long branches.

31
00:02:10.093 --> 00:02:14.253
It carries signals over long distances, in some cases about a metre.

32
00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:17.843
A muscle cell in your arm is long and thin.

33
00:02:19.123 --> 00:02:20.543
It shortens to pull on bones.

34
00:02:21.903 --> 00:02:24.303
Three cells, three shapes, each fitting its job.

35
00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.267
Now zoom back down the levels.

36
00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.307
That heart muscle cell is still a cell.

37
00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:37.007
But it sits inside every level above it: a tissue, the heart, the circulatory system

38
00:02:37.187 --> 00:02:38.187
and you.

39
00:02:38.517 --> 00:02:41.297
Sharing the work like this is division of labor.

40
00:02:42.677 --> 00:02:46.317
Each level does part of the job, and the levels depend on each other.
